    "tutorials":
    {
        "basic":
        {
            "id": "basic",
            "title": "Basic",
            "decks":
            {
                "id": "decks",
                "title": "Decks",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "Before starting a Duel, you must have a deck(s). There are 3 kinds of decks:",
                            "• Main Deck (must contain 40 - 60 cards): This deck contain all of your mainly used cards including Monsters, Spells, Traps,...",
                            "• Extra Deck (must contain 0 - 15 cards): This deck contain monsters that can be only Special Summoned. Those monsters can bring a huge advantage to your tactics.",
                            "• Side Deck (must contain 0 - 15 cards): For normal Duel, you don't need a Side Deck, but in standard Match which includes 3 Duels, after finish the first Duel, you will want to alter the contents of the Main Deck and Extra Deck to duel with opponent's deck(s). Therefor, you will need a Side Deck that contain cards which has special uses.",
                            "Notice:",
                            "Extra Deck and Side Deck are optional, so you can still play without them.",
                            "After altering your Main Deck / Extra Deck, the number of cards in each decks must remain the same"
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            },
            "playmat":
            {
                "id": "playmat",
                "title": "Playmat",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "A Yu-gi-oh Duel is conducted on a playmat, like the following one:"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "large-image",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/images/playmat.png"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "Deck Zone & Extra Deck Zone: Each players have 2 zones to place their Main Deck and Extra Deck. For Side Deck, player can place it an anywhere else.",
                            "Monster Zones: Where monsters are placed and battling.",
                            "Spell & Trap Zones: Where spells, traps are placed and activated.",
                            "Pendulum Zones: The leftmost and rightmost Spell & Trap Zones are also Pendulum Zones which used for placing Pendulum Monsters.",
                            "Field Zone: The zone used for placing Field Spell.",
                            "Graveyard Zone (GY): The zone of used, destroyed or discarded cards.",
                            "Extra Monster Zones: Two player share 2 Extra Monster Zones, although Main Monster Zones can also hold monsters from Extra Deck, but for Link Monsters, those must be placed in Extra Monster Zones."
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        "gameplay":
        {
            "id": "gameplay",
            "title": "Gameplay",
            "main-goal":
            {
                "id": "main-goal",
                "title": "Main Goal",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "Each player start with 8000 LP (Life Points). Whoever can reduce opponent's LP to 0 (by battling, or effects...) wins the Duel, if both players' LP become 0, it will be treated as a draw."
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            },
            "phases":
            {
                "id": "phases",
                "title": "Phases",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "A player's turn will include the following phases:",
                            "• Draw Phase: The turn player draw 1 cards from their Main Deck.",
                            "• Standby Phase: A transitional phase between the Draw Phase and Main Phase 1.",
                            "• Main Phase 1: The turn player can summon monster, activate or set spells, traps,...",
                            "• Battle Phase: Battle Phase: During this phase, turn player's monsters can attack and battle with your opponent's monsters. Unlike other phases which player must enter, player can choose to skip the Battle Phase.",
                            "• Main Phase 2: The same as Main Phase 1. If player skipped Battle Phase, the Main Phase 2 won't happen, of course...",
                            "• End Phase: The turn ends."
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            },
            "summoning":
            {
                "id": "summoning",
                "title": "Summoning",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "There are 4 types of summoning in Yu-gi-oh:",
                            "• Normal Summon: Place monster from hand to Main Monster Zones vertically and face-up."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "video",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/videos/Normal Summon.mp4"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "• Set: Place monster from hand to Main Monster Zones horizontally and face-down."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "video",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/videos/Normal Set.mp4"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "• Flip Summon: When a monster is already Set, player can flip it up (place it vertically face-up in the same zone). But, a monster cannot be flipped in the turn it was Set."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "video",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/videos/Flip Summon.mp4"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "• Special Summon: A type of summon which requires a special method or under specific conditions (can be placed either vertically or horizontally, face-up or face-down, by default, special summoned monsters must be face-up).",
                            "Notice:",
                            "Player can only Normal Summon or Set 1 monster once per turn, but can Flip Summon as many as possible if there is enough Set monsters.",
                            "There no limit for the times of Special Summon."
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            },
            "battle-mechanism":
            {

                "id": "battle-mechanism",
                "title": "Battle Mechanism",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "First, let's learn about Battle Position - it is the way that monsters was placed in the field:",
                            "• Attack Position: A monster is in Attack Position if it is placed vertically and face-up.",
                            " Face-up Defense Position: A monster is in Face-up Defense Position if it is placed horizontally and face-up.",
                            "• Face-down Defense Position: Monsters that was Set.",
                            "Of course, a monster can't attack unless it is in Attack Position. When a monster attack another monster. There can be 3 situation:",
                            "• If both are in Attack Position: Which monster with lower ATK will be destroyed (and sent to GY). The owner also lose LP equal to the ATK difference. If 2 monsters have the same ATK, both will be destroyed and players take no damage."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "video",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/videos/Attack-Attack.mp4"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "• If attacked monster is in face-up Defense Position: If attacking monster's ATK is less than attacked monster's DEF, it won't be destroyed, but the owner still lose LP equal to difference. If attacked monster's DEF less than attacking monster's ATK, it will be destroyed, but the owner won't lose any LP."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "video",
                        "source": 
                        [
                            "/source/videos/Attack-Defense-1.mp4"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "● If attacked monster is in face-down Defense Position: It must first be changed to face-up Defense Position, the rules will be apllied like the same above."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "video",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/videos/Attack-Defense-2.mp4"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "Notice:",
                            "A monster can only attack once per turn. While opponent control no monster, it can attack them directly and make them take damage equal to its ATK."
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            },
            "ways-to-win":
            {
                "id": "ways-to-win",
                "title":"Ways to Win",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "To reduce opponent's LP to 0, beside battling, there are some ways to do that:",
                            "• Using Spells and Traps: Some spells and traps have effect to deal damage directly to opponent.",
                            "• By monster effect: Some monsters also have effects to deal damage to opponent."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "medium-image",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/images/hinotama.png",
                            "/source/images/cannon-soldier.png"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "• Special Victory: Some card have special effects that can make player win when they meet its certain conditions."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "small-image",
                        "source": 
                        [
                            "/source/images/right-arm-of-the-forbidden-one.png",
                            "/source/images/exodia-the-forbidden-one.png",
                            "/source/images/left-arm-of-the-forbidden-one.png"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "small-image",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/images/right-leg-of-the-forbidden-one.png",
                            "/source/images/left-leg-of-the-forbidden-one.png"
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        "monsters":
        {
            "id": "monsters",
            "title": "Monsters",
            "monster-card":
            {
                "id": "monster-card",
                "title": "Monster Card",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "A normal Monster Card will include:",
                            "• Card Name",
                            "• Attribute - There are 7 attributes:"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "icon",
                        "content": 
                        [
                            {
                                "source": "/source/images/DARK.png",
                                "text": ""
                            },
                            {
                                "source": "/source/images/LIGHT.png",
                                "text": ""
                            },
                            {
                                "source": "/source/images/FIRE.png",
                                "text": ""
                            },
                            {
                                "source": "/source/images/WATER.png",
                                "text": ""
                            },
                            {
                                "source": "/source/images/EARTH.png",
                                "text": ""
                            },
                            {
                                "source": "/source/images/WIND.png",
                                "text": ""
                            },
                            {
                                "source": "/source/images/DIVINE.png",
                                "text": ""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "• Level (1 - 12): For monster that is Level 4 or lower, you can Normal Summon or Set it without Tributing (sent other monsters from field to GY) but for Level 5 / 6 monsters, you need Tributing 1 monster you control to Normal Summon/Set it (also called Tribute Summon). For Level 7 or higher monsters, you need tributing 2.",
                            "• Monster Image",
                            "• Monster Type",
                            "• Description (or Effect)",
                            "• ATK and DEF"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "large-image",
                        "source": 
                        [
                            "/source/images/Monster Card.png"
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            },
            "normal-monsters":
            {
                "id": "normal-monsters",
                "title": "Normal Monsters",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "Normal Monster is monster card with no effects and can be Normal Summon, which mean its description doesn't affect to the gameplay. Normal Monster Card is yellow colored, like this one:"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "medium-image",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/images/Normal Monster.png"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "Notice:",
                            "Not every monster that has no effects is Normal Monster. It must have the word \"Normal\" in its type, if not, it will be called \"non-Effect Monster\"."
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            },
            "effect-monsters":
            {
                "id": "effect-monsters",
                "title": "Effect Monsters",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": 
                        [
                            "Effect monster is monster that has special abilites (effects). Effect Monster Card is brown colored."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "medium-image",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/images/Effect Monster.png"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "This card's description says it couldnot be destroyed by battle with monster that has 1900 or more ATK. Which mean if this card attack (or be attacked by) a monster with 1900+ ATK, it won't be destroyed, but the owner still take the battle damage."
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            },
            "ritual-monsters":
            {
                "id": "ritual-monsters",
                "title": "Ritual Monsters",
                "content":
                [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "Ritual monster is monster that can be Special Summon (from hand) by using Ritual Spell and tributing monsters whose total Level equal or exceed to the Level of Ritual monster. Of course, this method of summoning is called \"Ritual Summon\". Ritual Monster Card is light-blue colored."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "medium-image",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/images/Ritual Monster.png",
                            "/source/images/Ritual Spell.png"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "To Ritual Summon, the player must activate Ritual Spell first, then sent the monsters (called \"materials\") from field and/or hand to the GY, then placed the Ritual Monster from hand to the field."
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "video",
                        "source":
                        [
                            "/source/videos/Ritual Summon.mp4"
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text":
                        [
                            "Notice:",
                            "Ritual Monster Card is inside the Main Deck, which mean player has to draw it before can summon it.",
                            "All materials must be face-up before being sent to GY."
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            },
